INT. LAUNDROMAT-CAFE "SUDS & BEANS" - MORNING

Machines hum. A chalkboard menu. Mismatched armchairs. Rain taps the windows.

SOFIA ABERNATHY-KHOURY, 30s, sits cross-legged in an armchair with a paperback and a latte. Across from her, in the next chair, THEODORE "TEDDY" LINDGREN-ASANTE, 30s, folds a stack of towels with great ceremony. He glances at her book. She glances at his towels. A dryer buzzes. Neither moves.

TEDDY
(quietly)
That's a good one.

SOFIA
You've read it?

TEDDY
Twice.

SOFIA
Everyone says the ending is a letdown.

TEDDY
Everyone's wrong.

Sofia closes the book on her finger.

SOFIA
What's your favorite part?

TEDDY
The part where nothing happens.

SOFIA
That's most of it.

TEDDY
Exactly.

She laughs. He looks pleased, then busies himself with a towel. The dryer buzzes again. This time he gets up, opens the door, and starts pulling out warm clothes. Sofia watches. He holds up a pair of socks, one blue and one yellow.

TEDDY (CONT'D)
(to himself)
How does this keep happening?

SOFIA
(overhearing)
It's a conspiracy.

TEDDY
It's entropy.

SOFIA
Same thing.

He sits back down with the clothes in his lap. She sips her latte. Rain keeps tapping.

SOFIA (CONT'D)
(to the room, lightly)
Anybody else feel like the whole city is just waiting?

A barista at the counter, unseen, clatters a cup. Teddy and Sofia look at the sound, then back at each other.

TEDDY
For what?

SOFIA
For someone to say something.

TEDDY
Maybe someone just did.

Sofia tilts her head. A dryer thumps. Teddy holds up the mismatched socks.

TEDDY (CONT'D)
Want one?

SOFIA
Which?

TEDDY
You pick.

She considers, then takes the yellow. She tucks it into her book as a bookmark. He tucks the blue into his pocket. They sit quietly.

SOFIA
What's your name?

TEDDY
Teddy.

SOFIA
Sofia.

They do not shake hands. They both look at the rain.

TEDDY
It's supposed to stop at noon.

SOFIA
I hope it doesn't.

He looks at her. She looks at her book. A dryer shuts off, and the room is quiet enough to hear the tick of the clock above the counter.

SOFIA (CONT'D)
(softly, to herself)
Stay.

TEDDY
Hm?

SOFIA
The weather. I meant the weather.

TEDDY
Oh. Right.

He smiles at his knees. She turns a page she isn't reading. Outside, the rain thickens.
